    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "CardBERT clusters by theme here as briefed: city-0 is 27 of 91 entries and is mostly 'is a Dinosaur', so its hoods carry the functional split. Verified-line cards: 3 in city-0 (2 in hood-0 incl. the commander, 1 in hood-1), 1 in city-1 hood-0, 1 in city-2 hood-1, 1 in city-5 hood-0.",
      "city-0-hood-2 (3 cards): Bronzebeak Foragers and Trapjaw Tyrant both exile-until-leaves; Monster Manual // Zoological Study is a put-from-hand artifact and reads as the odd member, closer in job to city-4-hood-1.",
      "city-0 holds Purphoros, Bloom Tender and Selvala, which are not Dinosaurs; Purphoros sits with the closers, which matches its role in the strategic frame.",
      "city-2-hood-1 includes Blasphemous Act, a symmetric sweeper, alongside creature-scaling sorceries; it is the one member that does not use your own bodies (beyond being cheaper with many creatures).",
      "city-3-hood-0 is two checklands plus Kessig Wolf Run, a utility land; the split from city-3-hood-1 is clean for the checklands (no basic types, not fetchable) and arbitrary for Wolf Run.",
      "city-4-hood-0 mixes fetches with tribal-type lands and Rogue's Passage; the shared thread is 'colourless-or-conditional lands', and Rogue's Passage is the odd member.",
      "city-5-hood-1 (Carnage Tyrant, Ghalta Primal Hunger, Hunting Velociraptor, Kinjalli's Sunwing, Wayward Swordtooth) shares no single job I can name; the split from hood-0 looks arbitrary, hence a deliberately loose label and no gloss.",
      "Hunter's Insight and Rishkar's Expertise in city-1-hood-1 are draw, not tutors; 'THE DIG' is chosen to cover both."
    ]
  },
